Q: How to add an ORDER BY clause using CodeIgniter query builder A: <p>I try this to solve:</p>

<pre><code>$data['aktivisdcm1'] = $this-&gt;db-&gt;order_by("nama", "asc")-&gt; get_where('tb_imam', array('status' =&gt; 'Aktivis'))-&gt;result_array(); 
</code></pre>

Q: Calling CodeIgniter&#39;s order_by() after get() does not sort the results A: <p>The problem is that: you execute the query before you ask to order it.<br>
Order before and then execute the query<br>
When you make: <code>db-&gt;get</code> you execute the query, if you have a where condition or an order condition you have to put it before the get command.<br>
Try this</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;order_by('published', 'ASC');
$pag = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('articles', $config['per_page'], $this-&gt;uri-&gt;segment(4));  
$data['records'] = $pag-&gt;result();
</code></pre>

<p><a href="http://ellislab.com/codeigniter/user-guide/database/active_record.html" rel="nofollow"><strong>DOCUMENTATION</strong></a></p>

Q: cargo site—slideshow gallery with thumbnail index A: <p>In this caso (let me know Cargo's version; but usually 2 or 3) you might need Javascript. Try adding this in the <code>Custom JS</code> tab:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script&gt;
document.addEventListener(&quot;DOMContentLoaded&quot;, function() {
    const mainSlideshow = document.querySelector('gallery-slideshow');
    const thumbGallery = document.querySelector('gallery-justify');

    if (!mainSlideshow || !thumbGallery) return;

    const thumbnails = thumbGallery.querySelectorAll('media-item');

    thumbnails.forEach((thumb, index) =&gt; {
        thumb.style.cursor = 'pointer';
        thumb.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
            e.preventDefault();
            e.stopPropagation();

            if (typeof mainSlideshow.setIndex === 'function') {
                mainSlideshow.setIndex(index);
            } else {
                mainSlideshow.setAttribute('active-index', index);
            }

            mainSlideshow.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
        });
    });
});
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If the gallery stall (stops or breaks), remove it and comment here.</p>

Q: How do I get a Minimal API to return a bool? A: <p>Make your API response generic so the type is preserved.</p>
<pre><code>    public class APIResponse&lt;T&gt;
    {
        public APIResponse()
        {
            ErrorMessages = new List&lt;string&gt;();
            Result = new object();
        }

        public bool IsSuccess { get; set; }
        public T Result { get; set; }
        public HttpStatusCode StatusCode { get; set; }
        public List&lt;string&gt; ErrorMessages { get; set; }
</code></pre>
